=begin
      author: Fizzleworth
        name: fizzlesson
        game: gemstone
        tags: sorcerer, guild, illusions, teach, learn, minor demon
    requires: Lich > 5.14.2
     version: 0.2
        note: Written with assistance from Claude (Anthropic).

  Helps with the Sorcerer Guild's Illusions teaching tasks, as the teacher, the
  student, or both at once (two sorcerers who both have a teach task can take
  turns teaching each other).

  Teaching: you lecture with ILLUSION TEACH <person> <illusion>; it counts once
  they do that illusion within about a minute ("[Your teaching of <Name> was
  successful.  You have N repetitions remaining.]"). fizzlesson lectures again
  after each success, and again after 75 seconds if it didn't count, until your
  task is done.

  Being taught: after "<Name> begins to meticulously lecture you ..." you have
  about a minute (55 seconds counted, 68 didn't) to do the illusion on your own
  minor demon. fizzlesson waits out the lecture's roundtime, dispels your demon's
  old disguise if it has one, and casts. It always targets your demon by its ID,
  because ILLUSION DEMON with a name or adjective can't tell two grantris apart
  ("Illusioning a demon that is not your own may not be a good idea") and finds
  nothing once your demon is disguised as a weasel or a ferret. Void lessons are
  done too (ILLUSION VOID, then POKE MY VOID) if you have a hand free; anything
  else it tells you to do yourself.

  The lesson doesn't have to be your latest illusion: a void lesson counted for a
  teach task at rank 55 (2026-11-04), and it's much less fiddly for the student.

  Usage:
    ;fizzlesson <name> [illusion]   teach <name> (default illusion: demon) until your
                                    teach task is done, and answer <name>'s lectures
                                    e.g. ;fizzlesson Asthenea void
    ;fizzlesson learn [name]        only answer lectures (from <name>, or from anyone)
    ;fizzlesson help

  ;kill fizzlesson stops it any time.

  changelog:
    0.2 (2026-11-04) command replies come through the script's own hook (0.1 never saw its
        lectures start, so it re-lectured into "You are already teaching"); the last rep's
        "You have completed your training task" ends the teaching
    0.1 (2026-11-04) first version
=end

module FizzLesson
  HOOK = 'fizzlesson_events'.freeze
  # Within this many seconds of a lecture, the student's illusion counted (55 s worked, 68 s
  # didn't, 2026-11-04)
  WINDOW = 55
  # How long the teacher waits for a lecture to count before lecturing again
  RELECTURE_AFTER = 75
  MAX_MISSES = 3

  LECTURED_ME = /^(\w+) begins to meticulously lecture you on the various intricacies of (.+?)\.(?:\s|$)/
  # The void lesson reads "Making sure Asthenea is paying close attention, you explain the
  # subtleties of creating the illusion of a dark black void in the palm of your hand." for the
  # teacher (verified); the student's side is a guess from that.
  VOID_LECTURED_ME = /(?:^|, )([A-Z][\w'-]+) explains the subtleties of creating the illusion of (.+?) in the palm of/
  # "[Your teaching of Asthenea was successful.  You have 1 repetition remaining.]", and on the
  # last one "[Your teaching of Asthenea was successful.  You have completed your training task.]"
  TEACH_OK = /\[Your teaching of (\w+) was successful\.\s+You have (?:(\d+|no) repetitions? remaining|completed your training task)\.\]/
  TASK_DONE = /\[You have completed your training task\.\]/
  LECTURE_STARTED = /^You meticulously begin to lecture|^Making sure \w+ is paying close attention, you explain the subtleties/
  # "You are already teaching Asthenea.  Wait a few seconds and try again." means the last
  # lecture is still open: she hasn't done the illusion yet
  ALREADY_TEACHING = /^You are already teaching/
  TEACH_REPLY = Regexp.union(
    LECTURE_STARTED,
    ALREADY_TEACHING,
    /trying to teach\?/,
    /^You (?:can(?:'|no)t|must|need|don't|are not|aren't|have no)\b/,
    /^(?:\w+) (?:is not|isn't|doesn't|does not|has no|already)\b/
  )
  CAST_REPLY = /Piece by piece, the creature's form changes until|is already illusioned|I could not find what you were referring to|not your own|You don't|You can't|You need/
  DISPEL_REPLY = /With a flick of your hand|I could not find what you were referring to|not your own|isn't|is not|You don't|You can't/
  VOID_REPLY = /rippling black void|void slowly opens|You (?:need|don't|can't)|free hand/
  WAIT_LINE = /^\.\.\. ?wait (\d+) sec/

  # Same noun patterns as fizzarts' Illusions.demon_type (gswiki Minor demon messaging); a noun
  # that matches none of them is a disguise (gnoll, raven, ferret, weasel, ermine, ...)
  DEMON_NOUNS = {
    'igaesha'  => /\A(?:haze|rouk|brume|haar|murk|nyle|mist|smoke|vapor|fog)\z/,
    'imp'      => /\Aimp\z/,
    'shien'    => /\A(?:darkling|shadowling)/,
    'verlok'   => /\Averlok/,
    'grantris' => /\Agrantris/,
    'aishan'   => /\Aaishan/,
    'arashan'  => /\Aarashan/,
    'abyran'   => /\Aabyran/,
    'grik'     => /\Agrik/,
  }.freeze

  def self.msg(text, color = :info)
    if color == :warn
      _respond("<pushBold/>[fizzlesson] #{text.gsub('&', '&amp;').gsub('<', '&lt;').gsub('>', '&gt;')}<popBold/>")
    else
      respond "[fizzlesson] #{text}"
    end
  end

  def self.help
    respond
    respond 'fizzlesson: Sorcerer Guild Illusions teach/learn helper'
    respond
    respond '  ;fizzlesson <name> [illusion]   teach <name> (default: demon) until your teach'
    respond '                                  task is done, and answer their lectures too'
    respond '  ;fizzlesson learn [name]        only answer lectures (from <name>, or anyone)'
    respond '  ;fizzlesson help                this help'
    respond
    respond '  As the student it waits out the lecture roundtime, dispels your demon\'s old'
    respond '  disguise, and casts ILLUSION DEMON on your own demon by its ID, so another'
    respond '  sorcerer\'s grantris (or ermine) in the room can\'t get in the way. You have'
    respond '  about a minute after a lecture. Void lessons are done too if a hand is free.'
    respond
    respond '  The lesson needn\'t be your latest illusion: void counts for the teach task,'
    respond '  and it\'s far less fiddly for the student (;fizzlesson <name> void).'
    respond
    respond '  As the teacher it lectures, waits for "[Your teaching of <Name> was'
    respond "  successful...]\", and lectures again; after #{RELECTURE_AFTER} seconds without one it"
    respond "  lectures again, and stops after #{MAX_MISSES} in a row."
    respond
  end

  # ---- events from the game -------------------------------------------------------------------

  # Command replies are caught here too (see command), as well as the lesson events
  def self.start_hook
    @events = Queue.new
    @expect = nil
    @reply = nil
    @wait_secs = nil
    DownstreamHook.remove(HOOK)
    DownstreamHook.add(HOOK, proc { |xml|
      begin
        xml.to_s.split("\n").each { |raw|
          line = raw.gsub(/<[^>]+>/, '').gsub('&gt;', '>').gsub('&lt;', '<').gsub('&amp;', '&').strip
          if (want = @expect)
            if line =~ WAIT_LINE
              @wait_secs = Regexp.last_match(1).to_i
            elsif @reply.nil? && line =~ want
              @reply = line
            end
          end
          if line =~ LECTURED_ME || line =~ VOID_LECTURED_ME
            @events << [:lectured, Regexp.last_match(1), Regexp.last_match(2), Time.now]
          elsif line =~ TEACH_OK
            @events << [:taught, Regexp.last_match(1), Regexp.last_match(2) || 'no']
          elsif line =~ TASK_DONE
            @events << [:task_done]
          end
        }
      rescue StandardError
        nil
      end
      xml
    })
    before_dying { DownstreamHook.remove(HOOK) }
  end

  # Sends cmd and returns the first game line matching pattern ('' if none came within timeout
  # seconds), resending after a "...wait N seconds." The reply is read by our own DownstreamHook,
  # not get?: on 2026-11-04 dothistimeout in this script never saw a single reply (it didn't even
  # retry on "...wait 1 seconds."), while the hook caught every line.
  def self.command(cmd, pattern, timeout = 5)
    4.times do
      waitrt?
      @reply = nil
      @wait_secs = nil
      @expect = pattern
      put cmd
      deadline = Time.now + timeout
      sleep 0.1 until @reply || @wait_secs || Time.now > deadline
      break unless @reply.nil? && @wait_secs

      sleep [@wait_secs - 0.5, 0.3].max
    end
    reply = @reply.to_s
    @expect = nil
    reply
  end

  def self.next_event(timeout)
    deadline = Time.now + timeout
    loop do
      return @events.pop(true) unless @events.empty?
      return nil if Time.now >= deadline

      sleep 0.2
    end
  end

  # ---- guild status ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  # The Illusions task text and repetitions left, from GLD
  def self.illusions_task
    lines = Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml('gld', /You are (?:a|an) |You have no guild|You are not a member/)
    skill = nil
    task = nil
    reps = nil
    lines.each { |xml|
      line = xml.gsub(/<[^>]+>/, '').strip
      if line =~ /ranks? in the (.+?) skill\./
        skill = Regexp.last_match(1)
      elsif skill == 'Illusions' && line =~ /^The Training Administrator told you to (.*)\.$/
        task = Regexp.last_match(1)
      elsif skill == 'Illusions' && line =~ /^You have (\d+|no) repetitions? remaining/
        reps = Regexp.last_match(1) == 'no' ? 0 : Regexp.last_match(1).to_i
      end
    }
    [task, reps]
  end

  # ---- your minor demon -----------------------------------------------------------------------

  # [id, noun, name] of your minor demon (its noun is the disguise's while it wears one), or nil
  def self.read_demon
    lines = Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml('tell md to follow', /You have no minor demon at this time|You command your|is already following you|acknowledges your order/)
    lines.each { |line|
      if line =~ /(?:Your|You command your) <pushBold\/><a exist="(\d+)" noun="([\w,'-]+)">([\w\-' ]+)<\/a><popBold\/>/
        return [Regexp.last_match(1), Regexp.last_match(2), Regexp.last_match(3)]
      end
    }
    nil
  end

  def self.disguised?(noun)
    DEMON_NOUNS.none? { |_type, pattern| noun.to_s.downcase =~ pattern }
  end

  def self.wait_for_mana
    return if checkmana > 5

    msg "Waiting for mana (you have #{checkmana})."
    sleep 0.5 until checkmana > 5
  end

  def self.cast(id)
    wait_for_mana
    waitrt?
    command("illusion demon ##{id}", CAST_REPLY)
  end

  def self.dispel(id)
    wait_for_mana
    waitrt?
    result = command("illusion demon ##{id} dispel", DISPEL_REPLY)
    waitrt?
    result
  end

  def self.call_demon_back
    msg 'Your demon isn\'t here, so telling it to come back.'
    put 'tell mdemon return'
    sleep 10
  end

  # Being taught: do the illusion within the window after <teacher>'s lecture
  def self.answer(teacher, topic, lectured_at)
    return answer_void(teacher, lectured_at) if topic =~ /\bvoid\b/i

    unless topic =~ /demon/i
      msg "#{teacher} is teaching you #{topic}. fizzlesson only does demon and void illusions, so do this one yourself (you have about a minute).", :warn
      return
    end

    sleep 0.5 # the lecture's "Roundtime: N sec." comes right after it
    waitrt?
    demon = read_demon
    if demon.nil?
      msg 'You have no minor demon to illusion. Summon one (;summond <type>) and try again.', :warn
      return
    end

    id, noun, name = demon
    if disguised?(noun)
      result = dispel(id)
      msg "Couldn't dispel your #{name}: #{result.empty? ? 'no reply' : result}", :warn unless result =~ /With a flick of your hand/
    end

    result = cast(id)
    if result =~ /I could not find/
      call_demon_back
      result = cast(id)
    elsif result =~ /is already illusioned/
      dispel(id)
      result = cast(id)
    end
    waitrt?
    elapsed = (Time.now - lectured_at).round
    if result =~ /Piece by piece/
      late = elapsed > WINDOW ? " That may be too late to count (#{WINDOW} s counted, 68 s didn't)." : ''
      msg "Did the demon illusion #{elapsed} s after #{teacher}'s lecture.#{late}"
    else
      msg "The demon illusion didn't work (#{elapsed} s after the lecture): #{result.empty? ? 'no reply' : result}", :warn
    end
  end

  def self.answer_void(teacher, lectured_at)
    sleep 0.5
    waitrt?
    unless GameObj.right_hand.id.nil? || GameObj.left_hand.id.nil?
      msg "#{teacher} is teaching you the void, but both your hands are full. Free one and do ILLUSION VOID yourself (you have about a minute).", :warn
      return
    end

    wait_for_mana
    result = command('illusion void', VOID_REPLY)
    waitrt?
    elapsed = (Time.now - lectured_at).round
    if [GameObj.right_hand, GameObj.left_hand].any? { |hand| hand.name.to_s =~ /void/ }
      msg "Did the void illusion #{elapsed} s after #{teacher}'s lecture."
      put 'poke my void'
      sleep 1
      waitrt?
    else
      msg "The void illusion didn't work (#{elapsed} s after the lecture): #{result.empty? ? 'no reply' : result}", :warn
    end
  end

  # ---- teaching -------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  def self.student_here(name)
    GameObj.pcs.to_a.find { |pc| pc.noun.downcase.start_with?(name.downcase) }
  end

  # :started, :open (the last lecture is still waiting on the student), or :failed (after
  # saying why)
  def self.lecture(student, illusion)
    line = command("illusion teach #{student} #{illusion}", TEACH_REPLY)
    return :started if line =~ LECTURE_STARTED
    return :open if line =~ ALREADY_TEACHING

    msg "The lecture didn't start: #{line.empty? ? 'no reply (check the game window)' : line}", :warn
    :failed
  end

  def self.run(args)
    mode = :teach
    if args.first.to_s =~ /\A(?:learn|student|answer)\z/i
      mode = :learn
      args.shift
    elsif args.first.to_s =~ /\Ateach\z/i
      args.shift
    end
    partner = args.shift
    illusion = (args.shift || 'demon').downcase

    if mode == :teach && partner.nil?
      help
      return
    end

    start_hook
    partner = student_here(partner)&.noun || partner.capitalize if partner
    task, reps = illusions_task
    teaching = mode == :teach
    if teaching && task !~ /teach Illusions to/i
      msg "Your Illusions task isn't a teach task (#{task || 'none'}), so lectures won't count for you. Only answering #{partner}'s lectures.", :warn
      teaching = false
    elsif teaching && reps.to_i.zero?
      msg 'Your teach task has no repetitions left. Only answering lectures.', :warn
      teaching = false
    end
    learning = task.to_s =~ /teach you illusions/i

    if teaching
      msg "Teaching #{partner} #{illusion} (#{reps} to go), and answering their lectures. ;k fizzlesson to stop."
    else
      msg "Answering lectures from #{partner || 'anyone'}#{learning ? ' until your learn task is done' : ''}. ;k fizzlesson to stop."
    end

    misses = 0
    waiting_since = nil # when the current lecture started
    told_absent = false

    loop do
      if teaching && waiting_since.nil?
        student = student_here(partner)
        if student.nil?
          msg "Waiting for #{partner} to be here." unless told_absent
          told_absent = true
        else
          told_absent = false
          case lecture(student.noun, illusion)
          when :started
            waiting_since = Time.now
          when :open
            msg "Your last lecture to #{partner} is still open; waiting for them to do the illusion."
            waiting_since = Time.now
          else
            misses += 1
            if misses >= MAX_MISSES
              msg "#{MAX_MISSES} lectures in a row didn't work, so I've stopped teaching. ;fizzlesson #{partner} to try again.", :warn
              teaching = false
            end
            sleep 3
          end
        end
      end

      event = next_event(1)
      if event
        case event.first
        when :lectured
          _kind, teacher, topic, at = event
          answer(teacher, topic, at) if partner.nil? || teacher.downcase.start_with?(partner.downcase)
        when :taught
          _kind, student_name, left = event
          left = left == 'no' ? 0 : left.to_i
          msg left.zero? ? "#{student_name} got it: that was the last one." : "#{student_name} got it: #{left} to go."
          misses = 0
          waiting_since = nil
          if left.zero?
            msg 'Your teach task is done! Still answering their lectures; ;k fizzlesson when they\'re done.' if teaching
            teaching = false
          else
            sleep 2
          end
        when :task_done
          if learning && !teaching
            msg 'Your learn task is done.'
            exit
          elsif teaching
            msg 'Your teach task is done! Still answering their lectures; ;k fizzlesson when they\'re done.'
            teaching = false
            waiting_since = nil
          end
        end
      end

      next unless teaching && waiting_since && Time.now - waiting_since > RELECTURE_AFTER

      if student_here(partner)
        misses += 1
        if misses >= MAX_MISSES
          msg "#{MAX_MISSES} lectures in a row didn't count, so I've stopped teaching. Still answering their lectures; ;fizzlesson #{partner} to teach again.", :warn
          teaching = false
        else
          msg "#{partner} didn't get that one within #{RELECTURE_AFTER} seconds; lecturing again."
        end
      end
      waiting_since = nil
    end
  end
end

if Script.current.vars[1].to_s =~ /\A(?:help|-h|--help)?\z/i
  FizzLesson.help
else
  FizzLesson.run(Script.current.vars[1..].to_a.compact)
end
